[Music]  godzilla vs kong is nearly here and a  whole lot of man-made property is just  waiting to be smashed  exploded toppled set on fire or all of  the above at once  the world is waiting with bated breath  to see which giant creature emerges on  top once the dust clears or whether they  end up hugging it out and joining forces  against a larger threat  the monster movie to end all monster  movies drops in theaters and on hbo max  on march 31st  and if you have a place in your heart  for king size action you probably have  the date circled in red ink on your  calendar but will it be worth the wait  the plot of godzilla vs kong isn't  completely unknown  for one we already know why kong's  become godzilla's size since his much  smaller appearance in kong skull island  kong's the last of his kind but he's  still growing and you better hope he  does  because he we say once kong goes then a  big one comes up  reports from a godzilla vs kong set  visit and the movie's internet breaking  trailer have indicated that the face-off  between the two titans might very well  feature another threat that's more  mechanical in nature  mecha godzilla the legendary robotic  kaiju that's yet to make its monster  verse debut however whether the movie is  actually any good has remained a mystery  until now though you still have to wait  a while until the official reviews drop  the veil of secrecy is lifted enough  that the lucky few who have been able to  see the movie in advance are now allowed  to tweet their first impressions  it looks like fans of king kong and  godzilla can sleep easy because the  critic's early impressions indicate that  godzilla vs kong is everything you could  have ever wanted  and then some sean o'connell the  managing director of cinema blend  tweeted some extremely positive things  about the movie while also revealing  that some of the action takes place on a  hollow earth setting he wrote i had a  total blast with this movie  it gets wonky and weird and all of the  places a monster movie like this should  some of the human characters actually  work but it's the fights in hollow earth  that demand  a massive screen team kong shiraz  farouki of comic book debate confirmed  that the movie very much delivers on its  premise  and teased out audiences are in for some  seriously amazing action between the two  monsters  he tweeted godzilla vs kong is fun  vibrant action-packed and energizing it  lives up to the heavyweight match it  advertised with amazing visual effects  and action sequences  this movie is selling a spectacle and  that's exactly what audiences will get  bandango's managing editor eric david  agreed with that sentiment and also  pointed out that while big monster  action is obviously the draw here the  human cast is also great and the story  aspects hold water he wrote i've seen  godzilla vs kong and it is grade a  awesome the monster brawls are badass  and beautiful huge fights all well  designed and super gnarly solid story  strong cast really good score a true  midnight monster movie and my favorite  of the four modern godzilla kong movies  of course godzilla vs kong is no citizen  kane and some critics have pointed out  that when you take out the awesome  monster action scenes the rest of the  movie can feel somewhat lacking  jermaine lucia of gizmodo and io9  tweeted godzilla vs kong has excellent  action and effects the story is crazy  ambitious and at times achieve some  unique sci-fi coolness  i'd watch it again for that stuff but  most of the human angles are so  overstuffed illogical and pointless it  constantly took me out of it  collider's vinnie makuso enjoyed the  movie to the point that he stated  i'm going to watch this movie every day  that's available on hbo max turning the  volume on my television up a little bit  every time  however he noted that things aren't  exactly stellar when the story focuses  on humans  saying the human parts are still  bafflingly bad but the parts where one  giant monster wallops the other giant  monster in the face are incredibly good  the same outlets perry nemeroff also  pointed out the human plotline problem  though she felt that the talented cast  helps the issue  she wrote still don't think they've  nailed how to incorporate human  characters but the top-notch ensemble  helps while some critics seem to find  the human-focused bits of the movie  underwhelming it certainly seems that  godzilla vs kong is happy to be what it  is  a big fun lovingly crafted movie about  the two most famous giant monsters out  there duking it out  you'll get the chance to see how well  the movie succeeds in its mission when  godzilla vs kong is released in theaters  and on hbo max on march 31st  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the monsterverse are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  you

